WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:19.518
Hello! Who are you?

2
00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:23.542
I'm a great blue heron.

3
00:00:23.543 --> 00:00:27.468
Herons are waders.

4
00:00:27.469 --> 00:00:32.660
Those are birds that stay near shallow water.

5
00:00:32.661 --> 00:00:35.492
Where do you live?

6
00:00:35.493 --> 00:00:40.780
Great blue herons live in North America.

7
00:00:40.781 --> 00:00:47.559
We like rivers, ponds, marshes, and fields.

8
00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:50.561
What do you eat?

9
00:00:50.562 --> 00:00:56.517
We eat insects, mice, and even snakes.

10
00:00:56.518 --> 00:01:01.377
But we like fish best of all.

11
00:01:01.378 --> 00:01:04.626
How do you catch fish?

12
00:01:04.627 --> 00:01:11.272
We stand in the water without moving.

13
00:01:11.273 --> 00:01:16.152
We wait for fish to swim by.

14
00:01:16.153 --> 00:01:28.827
Then we use our sharp bills as spears.

15
00:01:28.828 --> 00:01:31.830
Do you lay eggs?

16
00:01:31.831 --> 00:01:36.716
We lay about five eggs at a time.

17
00:01:36.717 --> 00:01:41.723
We keep them in nests in high trees.

18
00:01:41.724 --> 00:01:44.931
Who are your enemies?

19
00:01:44.932 --> 00:01:49.121
We don't have many enemies.

20
00:01:49.122 --> 00:01:57.770
But raccoons and eagles sometimes eat young herons.

21
00:01:57.771 --> 00:02:03.535
You have really long legs.

22
00:02:03.536 --> 00:02:07.695
We have big wings too.

23
00:02:07.696 --> 00:02:14.226
We can spread them very wide.

24
00:02:14.227 --> 00:02:21.200
See? I look like a dinosaur in the sky!

25
00:02:21.201 --> 00:02:29.454
Good-bye, Great Blue Heron!
